1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,570
Chief, this way.

2
00:00:12,870 --> 00:00:13,830
Chief. Lord Qi.

3
00:00:14,170 --> 00:00:15,030
He's inside.

4
00:00:20,970 --> 00:00:22,000
Chief, please have some tea.

5
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:30,630
Too noisy.

6
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:37,530
Answer only what I ask.

7
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:39,400
If you dare drag anyone else into this,

8
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:40,470
I'll sever your tendons first,

9
00:00:40,470 --> 00:00:41,400
then flay your skin,

10
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:42,230
then cut off your hands and feet,

11
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:43,170
and leave you a limbless husk.

12
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:44,370
Let him speak.

13
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:45,630
Mercy, Your Grace!

14
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:46,470
Mercy, Your Grace!

15
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:48,070
You're no ordinary servant.

16
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:49,870
What is your relationship with Chen Lunda?

17
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:50,800
I...

18
00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:53,570
I was once a foot soldier in the Yulin
Border Cavalry.

19
00:00:53,770 --> 00:00:55,130
When Marquis Dingyuan was accused of
treason,

20
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:57,370
I was brought back to the capital for
trial.

21
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:58,200
Master.

22
00:00:58,970 --> 00:01:00,800
Chen Lunda had old ties with Marquis
Dingyuan,

23
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,600
so he saved my life.

24
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,900
You served under Marquis Dingyuan.

25
00:01:04,970 --> 00:01:06,470
The Yulin Border Cavalry had many
soldiers.

26
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:07,730
My rank was too low.

27
00:01:07,730 --> 00:01:09,170
I never... never met Marquis Dingyuan.

28
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:10,600
Speak up before His Grace.

29
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:12,330
I never met Marquis Dingyuan.

30
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:14,870
Chen Lunda sent you out that day.

31
00:01:14,870 --> 00:01:15,770
Who were you supposed to find?

32
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:17,170
I don't know either.

33
00:01:17,170 --> 00:01:18,630
He sent me to Wanjin Tower with a letter

34
00:01:18,670 --> 00:01:20,430
to a young master surnamed Chen.

35
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:23,970
Chen Huabai.

36
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:16,030
Chen Lunda truly raised himself a fine
son.

37
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,329
You again.

38
00:02:35,970 --> 00:02:37,900
My lord, what a coincidence. You again.

39
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,670
Why are you here?

40
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:47,230
Why are you here, my lord?

41
00:02:48,730 --> 00:02:52,270
Don't tell me you're up to no good too.

42
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,300
It's strange, really.

43
00:02:54,530 --> 00:02:57,000
Why do I always catch you when you're up
to no good?

44
00:02:57,130 --> 00:02:58,370
I spared your life last night,

45
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,900
yet today you dare come courting death
again.

46
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,300
Do you know sneaking into the palace at
night

47
00:03:03,570 --> 00:03:05,170
means being flayed and having your tendons
torn out?

48
00:03:05,370 --> 00:03:08,530
So palace trespassing gets you flayed?

49
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:12,400
Then for breaking into a court official's
residence,

50
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:14,730
what crime would that be?

51
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:19,400
We're no better than each other.

52
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:24,070
My lord, you took my headband.

53
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:25,570
You still haven't returned it.

54
00:03:29,170 --> 00:03:30,530
What do you think you are,

55
00:03:31,070 --> 00:03:32,470
acting so brazen before me?

56
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:35,670
So fierce.

57
00:03:36,770 --> 00:03:38,700
Looks like you can't bear to kill me.

58
00:03:39,430 --> 00:03:41,600
Fine. Then keep it.

59
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:44,400
Whenever my lord wishes to do it himself,

60
00:03:44,630 --> 00:03:45,900
I'll be waiting.

61
00:03:50,829 --> 00:03:51,630
Someone's coming.

62
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,200
Come with me.

63
00:04:12,970 --> 00:04:14,930
How is Lord Chen's health?

64
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:15,770
I'm fine.

65
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:17,430
It's all that Chu Mingke's fault.

66
00:04:26,330 --> 00:04:27,630
Be good, my lord.

67
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:31,830
Be sure to hide well.

68
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,930
The Western Depot truly is a mad dog.

69
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:37,300
We'd best act more carefully from now on.

70
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:39,570
I heard that eunuch dog arrested us

71
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:41,530
because of the Yulin Border Cavalry

72
00:04:41,530 --> 00:04:42,970
treason case from eighteen years ago.

73
00:04:44,530 --> 00:04:46,500
His Majesty has few heirs.

74
00:04:47,030 --> 00:04:48,170
Once Prince Sheng comes of age,

75
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:51,630
the Imperial Noble Consort and the Cabinet
will only grow bolder.

76
00:04:52,130 --> 00:04:54,400
Had the late empress and the Second Prince

77
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:57,170
not died in that fire because of Marquis
Dingyuan,

78
00:04:57,770 --> 00:05:01,100
the Second Prince would be of age now.

79
00:05:02,230 --> 00:05:04,070
Let go. Don't stay so close to me.

80
00:05:05,070 --> 00:05:06,170
It's so cramped in here.

81
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:08,200
If I let go, they'll find us.

82
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:10,570
My lord, desperate times call for
desperate measures.

83
00:05:10,570 --> 00:05:11,730
Bear with it.

84
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:12,430
The Shan clan

85
00:05:12,430 --> 00:05:13,470
The Shan clan

86
00:05:13,830 --> 00:05:14,700
were loyal martyrs to the last.

87
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:17,000
What loyal martyrs?

88
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,530
That faithful dog Chu Mingke

89
00:05:19,530 --> 00:05:21,530
should have died eighteen years ago.

90
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:23,430
Yes, yes. You're right, Lord Chen.

91
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,170
My lord, they're cursing you.

92
00:05:25,830 --> 00:05:26,930
And you're not angry?

93
00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:29,430
Why is your temper so awful with me?

94
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:36,730
What sound does a puppy make?

95
00:05:36,730 --> 00:05:38,070
Woof, woof.

96
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:42,870
Any progress on Prince Yu's return to the
capital?

97
00:05:43,270 --> 00:05:45,070
The Willow-Shooting Tournament is next
month.

98
00:05:45,330 --> 00:05:47,070
What if we use the tournament as an
opening

99
00:05:47,070 --> 00:05:48,700
and offer horses as tribute?

100
00:05:48,730 --> 00:05:50,800
The Cabinet will stop it at every turn.

101
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,230
Be good, my lord.

102
00:05:53,070 --> 00:05:54,500
Be sure to hide well.

103
00:05:56,970 --> 00:05:58,570
You'd better not let them find us.

104
00:05:58,800 --> 00:05:59,600
Don't you dare.

105
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,330
Would you like them to see you like this

106
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:02,930
coming out of a cabinet in the Chen
residence?

107
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:05,230
It seems you truly don't wish to live
today.

108
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:08,330
Then what does my lord plan to do with me?

109
00:06:08,570 --> 00:06:09,500
You...

110
00:06:10,730 --> 00:06:13,470
The day before yesterday, someone sent me
a secret letter.

111
00:06:13,930 --> 00:06:16,070
I'll fetch it for you to read.

112
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:26,200
Don't make a sound.

113
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,870
Here it is.

114
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:58,670
Take a look.

115
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:02,500
What is that?

116
00:07:03,870 --> 00:07:05,070
What is it?

117
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:08,530
You were rubbing against me just now.

118
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:10,200
What do you think it is?

119
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:12,670
You...

120
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:16,000
My lord, surely you won't refuse
responsibility?

121
00:07:16,670 --> 00:07:17,670
Do you want to die?

122
00:07:18,130 --> 00:07:18,930
Don't.

123
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:19,930
They'll hear us.

124
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:23,070
Don't be afraid. If they hear us, just
kill them all.

125
00:07:23,170 --> 00:07:24,900
That's what my lord does best, anyway.

126
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:27,670
It's getting late.

127
00:07:27,730 --> 00:07:29,500
I'll have someone escort you gentlemen
home.

128
00:07:29,570 --> 00:07:31,970
Then thank you, Lord Chen.

129
00:07:40,530 --> 00:07:41,370
My lord.

130
00:07:42,270 --> 00:07:43,270
Don't close your eyes.

131
00:07:44,370 --> 00:07:45,470
Look at me.

132
00:07:47,830 --> 00:07:49,370
I'll kill you first.

133
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:50,730
Please.

134
00:07:51,370 --> 00:07:53,200
Please, my lord.

135
00:07:54,330 --> 00:07:55,270
So hot.

136
00:07:57,370 --> 00:07:58,770
You... what's wrong with you?

137
00:07:58,870 --> 00:08:00,170
My dear lord,

138
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:01,930
guess.

139
00:08:25,330 --> 00:08:26,130
Who's there?

140
00:08:29,670 --> 00:08:31,430
Chief, what brings you here so late?

141
00:08:31,470 --> 00:08:32,600
I'll go fetch some water for you

142
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:33,370
so you can wash up.

143
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:38,730
Chief, your neck is wounded.

144
00:08:40,169 --> 00:08:41,130
How dare you.

145
00:08:41,530 --> 00:08:42,330
Mercy, Chief!

146
00:08:42,330 --> 00:08:43,070
Mercy, Chief!

147
00:08:43,070 --> 00:08:44,330
I didn't see anything.

148
00:08:44,330 --> 00:08:45,130
Please spare me, Chief!

149
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:52,530
Sir, where are you going?

150
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:55,470
Chief.

151
00:08:57,270 --> 00:08:58,300
Where have you been?

152
00:08:59,070 --> 00:09:00,800
I... I...

153
00:09:04,930 --> 00:09:06,270
I asked where you've been.

154
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:07,170
Chief.

155
00:09:07,170 --> 00:09:08,270
I asked where you've been.

156
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:10,270
Cut that thing off him.

157
00:09:10,270 --> 00:09:10,730
Yes.

158
00:09:11,170 --> 00:09:11,630
Chief!

159
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:13,770
Chief!

160
00:09:13,770 --> 00:09:14,730
Chief, I was wrong!

161
00:09:15,130 --> 00:09:15,930
I was wrong!

162
00:09:17,270 --> 00:09:18,100
Chief!

163
00:09:25,470 --> 00:09:26,270
Disgusting.
